# Line endings are pinned so that a clone reproduces dist/ byte for byte.
#
# This repository publishes generated files: Cloudflare Pages serves whatever a clone
# of dist/ contains, and tools/check.mjs compares those bytes against the source cache.
# A checkout that rewrites LF to CRLF would therefore serve - and validate - a document
# nobody built, with every text file a few hundred bytes heavier than the mirror reported.
#
# The machine-wide default here is core.autocrlf=true, so without this file git would do
# exactly that on every Windows clone and quietly change the deployed bytes.
#
# `-text` means: store and check out the bytes as they are, no conversion, for everything.
# The explicit binary group exists so git never spends its line-ending heuristics on a
# font or an image, and `whitespace=never` keeps diffs from complaining about trailing
# spaces in markup copied from WordPress, which we must not "fix".
* -text

# Media and fonts: never treat as text, never diff.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.otf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary

# Trailing whitespace is data we inherited from the source, not a style problem.
* whitespace=never
